title: Media
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: media_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; media_timer += 6;
card-image: img/media.jpg
#subtitle: Setting the direction for our media strategy.

= Media

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> runs a veritable media empire, with many newspapers throughout every German city and region. We could use the media for various purposes...

- @guardian
- @bbc
- @labourlist
- @socialmedia
- @socialmedia_2
- @socialmedia_3
- @socialmedia_4
- @return: We should not do anything with media at the moment.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@guardian
title: A major Guardian op-ed to bring on board <span style="color: #FFDF00;">Centrist Dads</span>.
subtitle: This might upset ideological purists, but it may bring in one-off donations and win over some of the PMC.
on-arrival: resources += 1; commercialized_media += 1; new_middle_spd += 4*(1 - dissent); old_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; socialism += 2*(1 - dissent); pro_republic += 1*(1-dissent); nationalism -= 1*(1 - dissent);

Our commercialized newspapers are able to bring in more funds. However, the left and labor factions express their displeasure.

@bbc
title: A One Show interview to put us in every living room in the country.
subtitle: Talking alotments with Matt Baker.
on-arrival: campaign_media += 1; workers_spd += 4*(1 - dissent); unemployed_spd += 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent) if new_middle_conscious == 1; rural_spd += 2*(1-dissent) if rural_conscious == 1

Our campaign media is mostly reaching the workers [? if rural_conscious == 1: and peasants ?] who are already saturated with <span style="color: #c00000;">Socialist</span> propaganda, but it must be doing *something*, or at least that is what we hope.

@labourlist
title: Get Labourlist to send a puff piece to activists' inboxes, to quell dissent on the right of the paty.
subtitle: There will be space for all factions to air their views.
on-arrival: labor_dissent -= 6; center_dissent -= 6; reformist_dissent -= 6; neorevisionist_dissent -= 6

The Labour Right, Blue Labour, Tribune Group and 'True Soft Left' factions are appeased.

@socialmedia
title: Social Media
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: radio = 0
on-arrival: radio += 1; resources -= 2; unemployed_spd += 4*(1 - dissent); workers_spd += 2*(1 - dissent); labor_dissent += 5; socialism += 3*(1 - dissent);  nationalism -= 1*(1 - dissent); nationalism -= 2*(1 - dissent) if pacifism > 1; pro_republic += 2*(1-dissent)

Build up social media to reach untapped demographics, and build up party membership. This will increase income from annual membership subs.

@socialmedia_2
title: Continue building up social media
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: radio > 0 and radio <= 3
on-arrival: radio += 1; resources -= 1; new_middle_spd += 5*(1 - dissent); old_middle_spd += 3*(1 - dissent); workers_spd += 3*(1 - dissent); socialism += 3*(1 - dissent); nationalism -= 1*(1 - dissent); nationalism -= 2*(1 - dissent)*(pacifism-2) if pacifism > 2; pro_republic += 2*(1-dissent)

Our new radio network has a mix of popular and political programming, and is proving a success.

@socialmedia_3
title: Continue building up social media
subtitle: It is now financially self-sufficient, and does not require any more resources.
view-if: radio > 3 and radio <= 5 and year <= 1931
on-arrival: radio += 1; new_middle_spd += 5*(1 - dissent); old_middle_spd += 4*(1 - dissent); workers_spd += 4*(1 - dissent); rural_spd += 3*(1 - dissent); unemployed_spd += 2*(1-dissent); socialism += 3*(1 - dissent); nationalism -= 1*(1 - dissent); nationalism -= 2*(1 - dissent)*(pacifism-2) if pacifism > 2; pro_republic += 2*(1-dissent)

Our radio network has become a successful tool for spreading our message.

@socialmedia_4
title: We should keep on supporting our radio network.
subtitle: As radio becomes more common, the novelty is beginning to wear off, and radio is becoming saturated in society. -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: radio > 3 and (radio >= 6 or year >= 1932) and radio <= 9
on-arrival: radio += 1; resources -= 1; new_middle_spd += 3*(1 - dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1 - dissent); workers_spd += 3*(1 - dissent); rural_spd += 2*(1 - dissent); unemployed_spd += 2*(1-dissent); socialism += 2*(1 - dissent); nationalism -= 1*(1 - dissent); nationalism -= 2*(1 - dissent)*(pacifism-2) if pacifism > 2; pro_republic += 2*(1-dissent)

We are continuing to invest in our radio stations. Both commercial and political radio are becoming more prevalent, making it harder to spread our message amidst the competition.
